{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Control Structure.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Control Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"control structure control structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Control Structure.md","fileName":"Control Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Control Structure","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Algorithm Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algorithm Foundations","Algorithm","Sequence Control Structure","Selection Control Structure","Iteration Control Structure","algorithms.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Control Structure.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Control Structure.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"control structure control structure","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Control Structure.md","fileName":"Control Structure.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Control Structure","heading":"Control Structure","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A control structure determines how the steps of an [[Algorithm]] or program are combined and which step executes next. Three forms are sufficient to organize algorithmic procedures: [[Sequence Control Structure|sequence]], [[Selection Control Structure|selection]], and [[Iteration Control Structure|iteration]].\n\nSequence places steps one after another. Selection chooses between alternatives according to a condition. Iteration repeats steps until a stopping condition is satisfied. Complex algorithms arise from nesting and composing these basic structures rather than requiring fundamentally different forms of control.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algorithm Foundations","Algorithm","Sequence Control Structure","Selection Control Structure","Iteration Control Structure","algorithms.epub"],"properties